  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Lincoln Ridge Park — known to locals as Banklick — is a 24-hole course in Independence, Kentucky, with a good mix of wooded and open holes across varied terrain and elevation. From the white tees it plays 6,943 feet at par 72, with a lake, a road, and a creek all in play as OB.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Chainstar baskets, it's the friendly marathon of the Cincinnati area — 24 par 3s that flow through the park without ever feeling repetitive. Not cart friendly, so plan to walk it.",
    "It's the course where the region's intermediate players get their 24-hole fix, and the OB hazards keep every round interesting."
